// Experimental.Fuzz and Experimental.FuzzSimulation from a .vibe program, with
// no import: a schema is accepted where an Arbitrary is, a needle behind two
// observations is found and shrunk, a finding replays from its token, a corpus
// store keeps confirmed failures, a store that fails is a FuzzError, and the
// simulation finds a lost update and a deadlock.

// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#summary | This VIP ports it unchanged and adds one convenience: a Vibe `schema` is accepted where an `Arbitrary` is.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#module | `Experimental.Fuzz` and `Experimental.FuzzSimulation`, in scope with no import.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#module | Their code is `vibelang-runtime/experimental/Fuzz`.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#module | | `Fuzz.run(input, property, options?)` | Run a campaign.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#module | `input` is a schema or an `Arbitrary`.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#module | | `Fuzz.target(input, property, { id, revision, codec? })`, `Fuzz.runTarget(target, options)` | A property with a stable identity, so a corpus store can keep its failures between runs |
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#module | | `Fuzz.observe(label)` | Record that execution reached a stage.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#module | | `Fuzz.score(label, value)` | A number to maximize, which turns a needle into a hill |
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#module | | `Fuzz.formatReport(report)` | A printable diagnostic, or `undefined` when the run passed |
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#module | | `Fuzz.Corpus` | The service that stores inputs and confirmed failures |
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#module | | `FuzzSimulation.execution()` | An execution mode in which fiber scheduling and time are fuzzed |
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#module | Options of `Fuzz.run`: `seed`, `executions`, `duration`, `plateau`, `maxFindings`, `feedback`, `execution`, `replay`.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#rules | **The property contract is `Arbitrary.checkEffect`'s.** Return `true`, or an Effect of `true`, to pass.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#rules | **A run stops at the first of** `duration` (10 seconds when no budget is given), `executions`, `plateau` and `maxFindings` (1 by default).
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#rules | **Feedback comes from five sources**: spans, on by default; the exit tag and each error tag; `Fuzz.observe` labels; `Fuzz.score` values; and the structure of the generated input.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#rules | **A finding has a signature**: `ReturnedFalse`, `PropertyError:<tag>`, `Died:<constructor>` or `Deadlock`.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#rules | **A finding replays.** `finding.replay` is a token holding the generator tape, the schedule tape and the shrink path.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#rules | `Fuzz.run(input, property, { replay })` reproduces it.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#rules | Kept inputs are a search cache tied to `revision`.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#rules | **Simulation is a closed world.** Under `FuzzSimulation.execution()`, each execution has its own scheduler and a virtual clock that jumps to the next timer when nothing can run.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#rules | A program with nothing runnable, no pending timer and an unfinished property is a `Deadlock` finding.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#claudes-decisions | `Experimental.Fuzz` and `Experimental.FuzzSimulation`, in scope with no import.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#claudes-decisions | Their code is `vibelang-runtime/experimental/Fuzz`.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#claudes-decisions | Call `Fuzz.run(input, property, options?)`: Meaning: Run a campaign.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#claudes-decisions | `input` is a schema or an `Arbitrary`.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#claudes-decisions | Call `Fuzz.target(input, property, { id, revision, codec? })`, `Fuzz.runTarget(target, options)`: Meaning: A property with a stable identity, so a corpus store can keep its failures between runs.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#claudes-decisions | Call `Fuzz.observe(label)`: Meaning: Record that execution reached a stage.
// rule-evidence: docs/design/vips/0070-std-fuzz.md#claudes-decisions | Call `Fuzz.score(label, value)`: Meaning: A number to maximize, which turns a needle into a hill.
